<div id="editorial-policy" class="editorial-box">
  <div class="editorial-header">Editorial Policy, Methodology & Research Standards</div>
  <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: #cbd5e1; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
    <strong>Author:</strong> {SITE.author} &bull; <strong>Publication Date:</strong> {SITE.publishedDate} &bull; <strong>Last Updated:</strong> {SITE.lastUpdated}
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #94a3b8; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
    Our editorial team independently researches and documents account security protocols, anti-fraud standards, and platform mechanics across live streaming platforms. We do not accept payment to rate or recommend unsafe tools, fraudulent mod APKs, or credential phishing sites. All technical explanations regarding WebSocket protocols, SSL/TLS token accounting, and server-side balance architecture are reviewed against industry cybersecurity baselines.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #94a3b8; margin-bottom: 0;">
    <strong>Authoritative Security Sources Consulted:</strong>
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/seo-starter-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Search Central Webmaster Standards</a>,
    <a href="https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/how-recognize-and-avoid-phishing-scams" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Federal Trade Commission (FTC) Phishing Guidance</a>, and
    <a href="https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CISA Cyber Hygiene Guidelines</a>.
  </p>
</div>
